# Terminal News Assistant — environment configuration template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for any sources you want to enable.
# .env is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
# Do NOT place real credentials in this file.

# ---- Phase 2: Reddit credentials ----
# Register a free "script" app at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps
# to obtain your client ID and secret.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=terminal-news-assistant/0.1

# If REDDIT_CLIENT_ID or REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET are blank, Reddit is skipped
# and the application continues with the other available sources.

# ---- Phase 5: Optional LLM Synthesis (OpenRouter or OpenAI) ----
# Provide an OpenRouter API key (recommended) or direct OpenAI API key
# to enable grounded natural-language synthesis.
# If left blank or unset, AI synthesis is skipped and the assistant operates
# as a pure multi-source aggregator at zero cost.
#
# Option A: OpenRouter (supports multiple models: gpt-4o-mini, claude, llama, deepseek, etc.)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
#
# Option B: Direct OpenAI API Key
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
